abstract: >-
  A weighted self-diagnostic that surfaces structural ambiguities in how
  an enterprise articulates its institutional logic, covering trade-offs,
  decision boundaries, digitalized meaning, ownership, governance, and
  delegation readiness, before AI systems are asked to operate against
  that logic. The assessment scores six dimensions on a 100-point scale
  and maps results to four readiness segments (Ready, Progressing,
  Emerging, Foundational) with segment-specific guidance on the work
  ahead. The assessment is the diagnostic entry point to the DSIL™
  framework and forms part of the Foundeon methodology.
